From 8c9398179e4c9f14f6a72bcd129ffb205b9efa53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:29:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] steam-frame client: the Frame's controllers as themselves,
 and the aim pose

The client now enables XR_VALVE_frame_controller_interaction when SteamVR offers it and suggests
/interaction_profiles/valve/frame_controller_valve bindings, so SteamVR stops emulating Oculus Touch
for it. Through that emulation right B, X and Y arrived as one button, three of the left d-pad's four
directions as another, and the bumper as the trigger. Bound natively, each input arrives on its own.

Wire: TrackingPacket gains controllerProfile (1 = Frame) and touchState after gazeDirection, plus
ButtonFlags bits from 0x0800 for each Frame input. The A/B/X/Y bits keep the meaning SteamVR's own
Frame-to-Touch remap gives them, so a server that knows only Touch sees what it saw before.

Also fills the aim pose, which no Frame client sent: every app's pointer ray was the grip pose, about
40 degrees off where the controller points.

